    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **54 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, mapping points to a level. Changes:\n\n1. **`Memberships.java`** \u2014 added `membershipPoints(email, namesakeCount, householdSize, registrationDate)` computing points (start 0; +2 email, +1 namesakeCount==0, +2 household \u2265 3, +3 tenure > 365 days), plus a `membershipLevel(int points)` banding (1: 0\u20131, 2: 2\u20133, 3: 4\u20135, 4: 6+). The existing `membershipLevel(...)` overload now derives from points and additionally takes `householdSize`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping and updated the `membershipLevel` mapping to pass `householdSize`, so both fields are returned.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema property and updated `membershipLevel`'s description/constraints (max now 4) to reflect the points-derived banding. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field.\n\nAll five spec tests (Cp15, Cp23, Cp24, Cp39, Cp40) and the rest of the suite are green.",
