    "probe_text": "POST `/api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the V2 controller only lists owners). Here is everything that happens, in execution order. I've marked each step as a **[validation]** (can reject the request) or a **[side-effect]** (mutates state, derives a field, persists, or logs).\n\n## Before the method body\n\n1. **[validation] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **[validation] Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 the interface binds it as `@Valid @RequestBody`, so `OwnerFieldsDto`'s constraints run first:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)` (non-blank)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)` (non-blank)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - (`postcode`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, `sharesHousehold` have no field constraints)\n\n## Inside `addOwner` (in this exact order)\n\n3. **[side-effect]** Map the DTO to an `Owner` entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n4. **[side-effect + validation] Normalize address** (`normalizeAddress`, line 123): trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, expands street abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`); stores the result. **Rejects** with `InvalidAddressException` (400) if blank after normalization.\n5. **[validation] Reject future registration date** (`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`, line 125): if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Checked against the raw supplied value, before business-day adjustment. A null date is allowed.\n6. **[side-effect] Default the registration date** (lines 126\u2013128): if none supplied, default to `LocalDate.now()`.\n7. **[side-effect] Roll to a business day** (`toBusinessDay`, line 129): Saturday/Sunday move forward to Monday; weekday unchanged. Then stored on the owner (line 130). All later date-derived values use this adjusted date.\n8. **[validation] Daily owner limit** (`rejectDailyLimitReached`, line 131): if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry that business day as their `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n9. **[validation] City capacity** (`rejectCityAtCapacity`, line 132): if \u2265 50 existing owners are in the same city (case-insensitive, null treated as empty) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n10. **[side-effect + validation] Normalize telephone** (`normalizeTelephone`, lines 133\u2013134): strips spaces/dashes/brackets, applies E.164 (keeps `+` and country code if present, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`); stores the E.164 value. **Rejects** with `InvalidTelephoneException` (400) if not 8\u201315 digits or the national-number length is wrong for a fixed-length country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210).\n11. **[side-effect + validation] Normalize email** (`normalizeEmail`, lines 135\u2013136): null/blank \u2192 stored as `null`; otherwise trimmed and lower-cased then stored. **Rejects** with `InvalidEmailException` (400) if it doesn't match the email pattern, or `DisposableEmailException` (400) if the domain is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n12. **[side-effect + validation] Validate postcode** (`validatePostcode`, line 137): null/blank \u2192 stored as `null`; otherwise must be exactly 4 digits, and for a known region must fall in range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). **Rejects** with `InvalidPostcodeException` (400) otherwise. Stored exactly as supplied.\n13. **[side-effect]** Compute the `sharesHousehold` opt-in flag from the request (line 138).\n14. **[validation] Reject duplicate identity** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`, line 139): if any existing owner has the same normalized telephone **and** email (existing values re-normalized before comparison) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n15. **[validation] Reject duplicate household** (`rejectDuplicateHousehold`, line 140): unless `sharesHousehold` is true, if any existing owner shares the derived `householdId` (from last name + postcode) \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409). Owners with no postcode are never household duplicates.\n16. **[side-effect] Assign customer code** (lines 141\u2013142): derive region (`Localities.region` from postcode/city), then set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256(telephone + lastName)>`.\n17. **[side-effect] Set namesake count** (`countNamesakes`, line 143): number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n18. **[side-effect] Set bulk-signup warning** (`computeBulkSignupWarning`, line 144): `true` if > 80 owners already carry that business day.\n19. **[side-effect] Set household size** (`countHouseholdMembers` + 1, line 145): existing members of the same household plus this one.\n20. **[side-effect] Set soft-duplicate flags** (lines 147\u2013149): unless `sharesHousehold`, find the earliest existing owner with the same last name + postcode but a *different* telephone; set `possibleDuplicateOf` to that id (or null) and `possibleDuplicate` accordingly.\n21. **[side-effect] Persist** the owner (`clinicService.saveOwner`, line 150).\n22. **[side-effect]** Map the saved entity to `OwnerDto` (line 151) \u2014 this is where derived response fields like `membershipLevel` (and `ageBand`) come from the mapper.\n23. **[side-effect] Audit log** (lines 152\u2013154): emits an `AUDIT` line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n24. **[side-effect]** Set the `Location` response header to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging about the ordering, in case it matters to you:\n\n- The **future-date check (step 5) runs on the raw supplied date**, but the **daily-limit (8) and bulk-warning (18) counts key off the business-day-adjusted date** (step 7) \u2014 a weekend signup is counted against the following Monday.\n- **Telephone/email/postcode normalization (10\u201312) happen *after* the daily-limit and city-capacity checks (8\u20139)** but *before* the identity/household duplicate checks (14\u201315), which rely on those normalized values."
